From: PTT-dev
Subject: [PATCH] ramips: fix refclk pad-setup bit-OR typo inside 835 kernel patch

mt7628_refclk_setup() in the ralink-i2s driver (added by kernel patch
835) intends to set bit 5 of sysc reg 0x1364, but writes
"data |= ~(0x1 << 5)" which ORs 0xffffffdf into the register and
clobbers every other bit (GPIO1 pull configuration on MT7628).

835 is applied at kernel-patch time, after the base patch series runs,
so amend the patch file itself.

--- a/target/linux/ramips/patches-6.12/835-asoc-add-mt7620-support.patch
+++ b/target/linux/ramips/patches-6.12/835-asoc-add-mt7620-support.patch
@@ -798,7 +798,7 @@
 +	data &= ~(0x1 << 5);
 +	rt_sysc_w32(data, 0x1354);
 +	data = rt_sysc_r32(0x1364);
-+	data |= ~(0x1 << 5);
++	data |= (0x1 << 5);
 +	rt_sysc_w32(data, 0x1364);
 +
 +	/* set refclk output 12Mhz clock */
